<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Jasdan State</h1><p class="st-meta">1665 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Jasdan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The leading Kathi state of central Kathiawar, ruled by a Khachar Kathi Darbar from Jasdan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Jasdan was held by the Khachar clan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathi-people">Kathis</a>, a pastoral warrior people who gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> its name. The Khachars established their rule at Jasdan around 1665 and expanded it through the 18th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Darbar ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and grazing country, paying tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaekwads">Gaekwads</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/junagadh-state">Junagadh</a> before British protection after 1807. It was among the larger Kathi holdings, though few details of individual rulers are widely recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Jasdan merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960. It is now a town in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rajkot-state">Rajkot</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jasdan-state.jpg" alt="Jasdan State" width="320" height="212"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jasdan_state_flag.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1665 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jasdan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jasdan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=jasdan-state" aria-label="Jasdan State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6588 1364 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Jasdan State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6908 1620L7364 1601M6908 1620L7364 1602M6908 1620L6896 1610"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6896 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6908 1620h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6908 1620h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=jasdan-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
